A1. You might find this on a dollar in Scotland. ~ RUST
A5. This kind of joke might go in vaudeville. ~ STALE
A9. Where you often find good-looking calves. ~ BARN
A13. This fellow was always well loaded. ~ ATLAS
A14. This may prove your metal. ~ ORE
A15. A bad actor. ~ ROGUE
A16. This is often roasted. ~ VEAL
A17. A bad way to get. ~ STEAL
A19. A twentieth-century discovery. ~ LEGS
A20. Even a Scotchman will give you the sleeves to this. ~ VEST
A22. Where some people were very much put out. ~ EDEN
A24. This is a high-grade fellow. ~ SENIOR
A26. What the unspared rod does. ~ SMARTS
A28. A pronoun. ~ HE
A29. This was used in a parable and dug up by Matthew. ~ TARE
A30. A native of the Philippines. ~ MORO
A31. The fall guy. ~ PA
A33. This is mighty shady. ~ OAK
A35. What smart little Swedish boys become. ~ MEN
A36. You don't have to add much to get this. ~ ONE
A37. A bounder. ~ CAD
A38. This often goes over a girl's head. ~ SLIP
A40. Hunts. ~ SEEKS
A42. A cut-up. ~ CARD
A43. This is always going up. ~ TENOR
A45. Not much in Scotland. ~ WEE
A46. Members of an ancient order. ~ MONKS
A47. Help wanted. ~ SOS
A49. The drinks are on this. ~ BAR
A51. Where policemen do their daily dozin'. ~ BEATS
A53. Gains. ~ EARNS
A56. There isn't any more than this. ~ ALL
A58. This is the cat's. ~ RAT
A59. His brays aren't bonny. ~ ASS
A60. The objective she. ~ HER
A62. Close. ~ NEAR
A64. What the wise office-boy got. ~ RAISE
A66. Where the Cro-Magnon was at home. ~ CAVE
A67. How Horizontal 24 faces the world. ~ DAZED
A68. "Mother, where do little fish come from?" ~ ROE
A69. What your nose knows. ~ FUMES
A70. Take off. ~ SHED
A71. A musical study. ~ ETUDE
A72. One thing men and animals have in common. ~ DENS

D1. A mad thing to do. ~ RAVE
D2. Indian. ~ UTE
D3. The perfect husband. ~ SLAVE
D4. It's a gift. ~ TALENT
D6. This is often up in arms. ~ TOT
D7. This covers a lot of ground. ~ AREA
D8. Meadow. ~ LEA
D9. Spanish dance. ~ BOLERO
D10. Representative. ~ AGENT
D11. This just lies around. ~ RUG
D12. A bird of a home. ~ NEST
D17. These attract a lot of women. ~ STORES
D18. Good mixers. ~ LEMONS
D21. The home of a famous pair of twins. ~ SIAM
D23. It requires nerve to take this. ~ DARE
D24. The condition in which a bottle of Scotch leaves Canada. ~ SEALED
D25. A word overheard in JUDGE'S Subscription Dept. (Adv.) ~ RENEW
D26. What Kipling thought a good cigar was. ~ SMOKE
D27. Any good plug will give you these. ~ SPARKS
D28. Hard to find in Scotland (what would we do without Scotland?) ~ HOST
D32. What a figure artist does. ~ ADDS
D34. Your sisters and your cousins and your aunts. ~ KIN
D37. Two of these make a dance. ~ CAN
D39. You'll find Greta Garbo in one of these. ~ POSE
D41. This is pretty smooth. ~ EEL
D42. Whoopee juice in Tennessee. ~ CORN
D44. A beastly noise. ~ ROAR
D46. The bad boy of the gods. ~ MARS
D48. This has several good points. ~ STAR
D49. This is always at the bottom of things. ~ BASE
D50. They while away the hours. ~ HANDS
D51. This is hot stuff. ~ BLAZE
D52. You've got to do this to get going. ~ START
D53. Slowed up. ~ EASED
D54. This causes remorse. ~ SHAME
D55. You'd never do this before taking a bath. ~ DRESS
D57. One of the wives of Jacob. ~ LEAH
D61. If three's a crowd—what's two? ~ EVEN
D63. You'd better stop if you see this. ~ RED
D65. This should be made good. ~ IOU
D66. This is something for an old cow to think over. ~ CUD


